  steps:
    1. Pick grid dims 10-20 x 10-20
    2. Choose 2-5 distinct non-zero colors
    3. Place the target solid rectangle (2-3 x 2-4, area 4-12) away from boundary
    4. Place 0-2 larger solid rectangles (each >= 2x target area), no pixel overlap with target
    5. Place 0-2 non-rectangles by generating a filled rectangle then randomly removing 5-35% of pixels (keeping 4-connected), no pixel overlap with target
    6. Ensure bboxes may overlap but actual pixels never collide
    7. Verify target is uniquely smallest filled rectangle
